 # Deterministic LCG Noise Generation
 
-Also called: Linear Congruential Generator, Rng
+Also called: LCG, Linear Congruential Generator, Rng
 
 ## Overview
-Deterministic LCG Noise Generation is a pseudo-random number generator that produces normalized floating-point values in the range $[-1, 1]$ using linear congruential recurrence and bit-shifting normalization [S1, S2, unofficial]. It is used in volume rendering to provide deterministic noise for ray origin offsetting, thereby avoiding banding artifacts during ray marching [Parent]. It differs from hash-based PRNGs by relying on sequential state updates rather than spatial hashing, and from incremental methods by its fixed modular arithmetic structure [S1, S2, unofficial].
